Principal-part guardrail
------------------------------------------------------------------------
(q;q)_infty                    pole_order=0                note=product tail, cusp-side eta factor after q^(1/24)
1/(q;q)_infty                  pole_order=0                note=partition tail; eta^-1 has one fractional polar unit
Delta=q(q;q)_infty^24          pole_order=0                note=cusp zero, no pole
j(q)                           pole_order=1                note=single integral polar term q^-1
bad infinite polar tail        pole_order=infinite/illegal note=q^-1 + q^-2 + ...; not legal as a modular-function quotient

LRC14 translation
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. q-Pochhammer is the product carrier: local factors multiply.
2. Its reciprocal is the recursive partition tail: infinitely many positive q-coefficients.
3. The log derivative is the divisor-sum channel, matching the repo's sigma/mu/phi lanes.
4. A modular-function quotient is legal only when the negative q-powers are finite.
5. LRC packet analogue: all polar terms must be named residual debts: AP/GW, q-witness, F7, K33, etc.
6. A raw quotient that creates an infinite negative tail is not a theorem; it is uncontrolled residual debt.

