New proof target
------------------------------------------------------------------------
HYP-3078: For HYP-2963 packet rows, build a q-cusp ledger F_P(q).
Require: bounded finite principal part + nonnegative/certified tail + named polar exits.
If such ledgers cover all rows and polar exits discharge through existing sidecars,
the modular-cusp rule becomes a finite obstruction theorem rather than another analogy.
